Good thread so far. On speeding up the pipeline itself, I'd first profile before swapping components: cProfile or py-spy will often show the bottleneck is I/O or a quadratic loop, not parsing. Batching reads, streaming instead of loading whole files, and vectorising with NumPy or pandas usually pay off more than a parser change.

@tidal_raven54's point about parser speed is plausible for JSON-heavy workloads, but I'd want to measure it on your data before assuming the gain. I'm not certain how large the improvement will be for your case.

I'd also echo @pixel_marten64: whichever speedups you adopt, a randomised test suite over edge cases (empty inputs, nulls, odd encodings) will catch regressions a faster-but-subtly-different parser might introduce.

